B1 — api() silently swallows 204 responses [CRITICAL]
  TestSprite test: TC025 (Delete a budget and confirm removal)
  Root cause: api() always called res.json() even on 204 No Content, throwing
              SyntaxError on empty body. No try/catch in delete handlers meant
              the error was swallowed silently by React. Budget appeared undeleted.
  Affected: all three DELETE flows — budget, invoice, expense.

  Fix 1 — frontend/src/lib/api.ts (line ~136):
    + if (res.status === 204 || res.headers.get("content-length") === "0") return undefined as T;
      return (await res.json()) as T;

  Fix 2 — frontend/src/app/budgets/page.tsx — handleDelete:
    - await deleteBudget(id);
    - setEditingId(null);
    - await load();
    - await loadStatus();
    + try {
    +   await deleteBudget(id);
    +   setEditingId(null);
    +   await load();
    +   await loadStatus();
    + } catch (e: unknown) {
    +   alert(`Failed to remove budget: ${e instanceof Error ? e.message : "error"}`);
    + }

